 "plain_text": "<|message_model|><|content_text|>*Blade Runner* (1982) is a landmark science fiction film directed by Ridley Scott, set in a dystopian, rain-soaked Los Angeles of the future. The story follows Rick Deckard, a \"blade runner\" tasked with hunting down and \"retiring\" rogue bioengineered beings known as replicants. These artificial humans are nearly indistinguishable from real people, leading to a complex exploration of identity, humanity, and what it means to be alive.\n\nThe film is renowned for its atmospheric visuals, blending noir aesthetics with futuristic technology to create a haunting, immersive world. It remains a cornerstone of the cyberpunk genre and has had a lasting influence on science fiction",
